---
import BlogBase from "../../../layouts/BlogBase.astro";

const pubDate = "2026-09-20";

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "What is the Crosby G-2150 shackle?",
    a: "The Crosby G-2150 is a forged carbon steel screw-pin anchor (bow) shackle manufactured by The Crosby Group. It is one of the most widely used rigging shackles in industrial lifting, conforming to ASME B30.26 with a 5:1 design factor. The G-2150 is the galvanized/painted finish version; the S-2150 is stainless steel.",
  },
  {
    q: "What sizes does the Crosby G-2150 come in?",
    a: "The G-2150 ranges from 3/16\" (WLL 1/3 ton) to 9-1/2\" (WLL 400 tons) across the Crosby catalog. The most common field sizes are 1/4\" through 2\" (WLL 1/2 ton to 35 tons). Custom sizes and higher WLL models are available through Crosby distributors.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the WLL of a Crosby G-2150 1\" shackle?",
    a: "The Crosby G-2150 in 1\" (25 mm) pin diameter has a WLL of 8-1/2 US tons (7.7 metric tonnes). The design factor is 5:1, giving a breaking load of approximately 42.5 US tons. Always verify against the current Crosby catalog before use.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can the Crosby G-2150 be used in side-loaded applications?",
    a: "No. The G-2150 is a chain (dee) shackle with a narrow D-shaped body — it is designed for straight in-line pulls only. Side loading on a chain shackle can cause the dee to spread and the pin to cross-load, reducing strength below the marked WLL. For angular or multi-direction loading, use an anchor (bow) shackle such as the Crosby G-209 or G-2130, which are rated for angular loads through the bow.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should I mouse a Crosby G-2150 screw-pin shackle?",
    a: "Yes, for any application where the pin may unscrew under vibration, rotation, or movement. Thread a 2–3 mm wire through the pin hole across to the shackle body to prevent the pin backing out. For permanent rigging or overhead lifts, Crosby recommends bolt-type shackles (G-2130) instead of screw-pin.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the difference between the Crosby G-2150 and G-2130?",
    a: "The G-2150 uses a screw pin (faster to rig/un-rig, but can unscrew under vibration). The G-2130 uses a bolt, nut, and cotter pin for positive locking — required for overhead crane service, long-duration rigging, and applications where pin rotation is possible. Both are rated to ASME B30.26 at 5:1 design factor.",
  },
];

const wllRows = [
  ["3/16\"", "5 mm", "1/3", "0.15", "1.65", "0.75"],
  ["1/4\"", "6 mm", "1/2", "0.23", "2.50", "1.14"],
  ["5/16\"", "8 mm", "3/4", "0.34", "3.75", "1.71"],
  ["3/8\"", "10 mm", "1", "0.45", "5.00", "2.27"],
  ["7/16\"", "11 mm", "1-1/2", "0.68", "7.50", "3.41"],
  ["1/2\"", "13 mm", "2", "0.90", "10.0", "4.54"],
  ["5/8\"", "16 mm", "3-1/4", "1.50", "16.3", "7.43"],
  ["3/4\"", "19 mm", "4-3/4", "2.16", "23.8", "10.8"],
  ["7/8\"", "22 mm", "6-1/2", "2.95", "32.5", "14.7"],
  ["1\"", "25 mm", "8-1/2", "3.86", "42.5", "19.3"],
  ["1-1/4\"", "32 mm", "13-1/2", "6.12", "67.5", "30.6"],
  ["1-1/2\"", "38 mm", "17", "7.71", "85.0", "38.6"],
  ["2\"", "50 mm", "35", "15.9", "175", "79.4"],
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Product",
    name: "Crosby G-2150 Screw Pin Chain Shackle",
    description: "Alloy steel ASME B30.26 chain (dee) shackle, WLL 1/3 to 35 tons, 5:1 design factor. The G-2150 is Crosby's screw-pin chain shackle for straight in-line pulls — use G-209 or G-2130 for angular or multi-leg applications.",
    brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: "Crosby" },
    manufacturer: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Crosby Group" },
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: faqItems.map(({ q, a }) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      name: q,
      acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a },
    })),
  },
];
---
<BlogBase
  title="Crosby G-2150 Shackle: WLL Chart, Specs & Selection Guide"
  description="Complete Crosby G-2150 screw-pin anchor shackle reference: WLL from 1/3 to 35 tons, size chart, ASME B30.26 compliance, and comparison with G-2130 bolt-type."
  canonical="/brands/crosby-g-2150/"
  ogType="article"
  pubDate={pubDate}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbItems={[
    { name: "Home", url: "/" },
    { name: "Brands", url: "/brands/" },
    { name: "Crosby G-2150", url: "/brands/crosby-g-2150/" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full" style="background:#1e2030; color:#94a3b8; border:1px solid #2a2d3e;">Brand Reference</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/20">Crosby</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/20">Shackles</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/20">ASME B30.26</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3 leading-tight">Crosby G-2150 Shackle: WLL Chart, Specs & Selection Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 text-lg mb-8 leading-relaxed">The G-2150 is The Crosby Group's alloy steel screw-pin chain (dee) shackle. Its narrow D-shaped body is optimized for straight in-line connections — chain coupling, rod end attachments, and single-leg slings. For multi-leg bridle lifts or angular loading, use the anchor (bow) shackles G-209 or G-2130.</p>

    <div class="answer-box mb-8">
      <p><strong>Quick reference:</strong> The G-2150 is a chain (dee) shackle — narrow D-shaped body for straight in-line pulls only. Do not use it for multi-leg slings or angular loading; the dee body is not rated for side loads. For angular applications, select the anchor (bow) G-209 (screw pin) or G-2130 (bolt type). The G-2150 is the go-to choice for chain coupling and rod-end connections where a narrow profile is needed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-rc">

      <h2>Crosby G-2150 WLL Size Chart</h2>
      <p>All values from The Crosby Group catalog. WLL in US short tons and metric tonnes. Design factor 5:1 per ASME B30.26.</p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Pin Dia (in)</th>
            <th>Pin Dia (mm)</th>
            <th>WLL (US tons)</th>
            <th>WLL (metric t)</th>
            <th>Break Load (US tons)</th>
            <th>Break Load (t)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {wllRows.map(([pin_in, pin_mm, wll_us, wll_mt, bl_us, bl_mt]) => (
            <tr>
              <td style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; color:#f59e0b; font-weight:600;">{pin_in}</td>
              <td style="color:#64748b;">{pin_mm}</td>
              <td style="font-weight:600;">{wll_us}</td>
              <td>{wll_mt}</td>
              <td style="color:#64748b;">{bl_us}</td>
              <td style="color:#64748b;">{bl_mt}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p style="font-size:0.75rem; color:#475569;">Reference data only. Verify current ratings against The Crosby Group official catalog before use in safety-critical applications. Alloy shackles have different ratings.</p>

      <h2>G-2150 Key Specifications</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Type</td><td>Screw-pin chain (dee) shackle</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Material</td><td>Alloy steel, quenched &amp; tempered</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Finish</td><td>Yellow chromate or galvanized</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Design factor</td><td>5:1 (ASME B30.26)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Traceability</td><td>Heat code on body, WLL embossed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Standards</td><td>ASME B30.26, Federal Spec RR-C-271</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Temperature range</td><td>−40°F to +400°F (−40°C to +205°C)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pin type</td><td>Threaded screw pin — for bolt-type, use G-2130</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Chain Shackle (G-2150) vs Anchor Shackle (G-209 / G-2130)</h2>
      <p>The G-2150 is a chain (dee) shackle — the narrow D-shaped body suits straight in-line connections. The G-209 and G-2130 are anchor (bow) shackles with a round body for multi-leg slings and angular loading. Choose based on load direction, not just pin type.</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>G-2150 Chain (Dee)</th><th>G-209 / G-2130 Anchor (Bow)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Body shape</td><td>Narrow D — straight in-line only</td><td>Round bow (omega) — angular loads OK</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Side loading</td><td>Not permitted — dee may spread</td><td>Rated for angular loads through bow</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Multi-leg bridle slings</td><td>Not recommended</td><td>Preferred — bow distributes load evenly</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rig profile</td><td>Narrow — fits tight spaces, chain links</td><td>Wider — more clearance required</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pin locking</td><td>Screw pin (G-2150) — mouse for vibration</td><td>Screw pin (G-209) or bolt type (G-2130)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>WLL range</td><td>1/3 – 35 tons (common sizes)</td><td>1/3 – 120 t (up to 400 t catalog)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

    </div>

    <div class="cta-box my-8">
      <p class="text-white font-bold text-base mb-2">Verify your Crosby shackle selection with our calculator</p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-4">Enter your load weight, sling angle, and number of legs to get the minimum required shackle WLL — then cross-reference the G-2150 size chart above.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/shackle-size-calculator" class="accent-btn">Shackle Size Calculator</a>
        <a href="/sling-angle-calculator" style="background:#1e2030; color:#f1f5f9; font-weight:600; padding:0.5rem 1.25rem; border-radius:0.5rem; text-decoration:none; border:1px solid #2a2d3e; display:inline-block;">Sling Angle Calculator</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-rc">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqItems.map(({ q, a }) => (
        <details style="border:1px solid #1e2030; border-radius:0.5rem; padding:0.75rem 1rem; margin-bottom:0.75rem; cursor:pointer;">
          <summary style="font-weight:600; color:#f1f5f9; list-style:none;">{q}</summary>
          <p style="margin-top:0.5rem; font-size:0.9rem;">{a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 pt-8" style="border-top:1px solid #1e2030;">
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm font-semibold mb-3">Other brand references</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-sm">
        <a href="/brands/crosby-g-209/" class="cta-box block hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors" style="padding:1rem; margin:0;">
          <p class="text-white font-semibold">Crosby G-209</p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Alloy screw-pin anchor shackle</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/brands/crosby-g-2130/" class="cta-box block hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors" style="padding:1rem; margin:0;">
          <p class="text-white font-semibold">Crosby G-2130</p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Alloy bolt-type anchor shackle</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/lifting-chain-grades-explained/" class="cta-box block hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors" style="padding:1rem; margin:0;">
          <p class="text-white font-semibold">Chain Grades Guide</p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-0.5">G80 vs G100 WLL chart</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/rigging-inspection-checklist/" class="cta-box block hover:border-amber-500/40 transition-colors" style="padding:1rem; margin:0;">
          <p class="text-white font-semibold">Rigging Inspection Guide</p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs mt-0.5">ASME B30.9 rejection criteria</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-gray-600">Disclaimer: This page is an independent engineering reference. RiggingCalculators.com is not affiliated with The Crosby Group. Always verify specifications against the manufacturer's current catalog before use.</p>
  </div>
</BlogBase>
